{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.OptionBCountingTransfer","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.OptionBCountingTransfer","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUTraceCountHard.holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUTraceCountHard.holds","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The trace's exact value is `#P`-hard. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUTraceCountHard.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUTraceCountHard.mk","kind":"ctor","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUTraceCountHard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUTraceCountHard","kind":"class","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L89-L95","doc":"**What the QOU trace gives, honestly (Option B, no instance).**  Its exact\nevaluation is `#P`-hard; that is counting-hardness, and it is *all* the\ntrace supplies.  The step to `P ≠ NP` is a separate decision lower bound\n(`generic_transfer_false` shows it is not automatic), left open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.traceCountHard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.traceCountHard","kind":"opaque","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L86-L87","doc":"The exact observation trace `J_L(q₀)` is `#P`-hard (JVW at non-torsion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.generic_transfer_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.generic_transfer_false","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L76-L84","doc":"**The generic counting→decision transfer is FALSE (sorry-free).**  Perfect\nmatching has a `#P`-hard count *and* a poly-time decision, so\ncounting-hardness cannot imply decision-hardness in general.  Hence any QOU\nroute from \"trace is `#P`-hard\" to \"`P ≠ NP`\" must use QOU-specific\nstructure — it can never be the generic principle.  This is why Option A's\ndegree-0 identification, read as a general law, is refuted, and why a\n*non-fiat* transfer needs a genuine decision lower bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.GenericTransfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.GenericTransfer","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L71-L74","doc":"A **generic** counting→decision transfer would assert, for the matching\nproblem, that its `#P`-hard count forces its decision to be hard (i.e. not\neasy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.MatchingFacts.decision_easy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.MatchingFacts.decision_easy","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L69-L69","doc":"König: matching *existence* is decidable in polynomial time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.MatchingFacts.count_hard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.MatchingFacts.count_hard","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Valiant: the permanent / matching count is `#P`-hard. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.MatchingFacts.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.MatchingFacts.mk","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.MatchingFacts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.MatchingFacts","kind":"class","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L62-L69","doc":"**Cited facts about perfect matching** (no instance — established, and\nMathlib has no `#P`).  Both hold simultaneously: a `#P`-hard count over a\npoly-time decision. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.matchingDecisionEasy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.matchingDecisionEasy","kind":"opaque","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L58-L60","doc":"Deciding whether a perfect matching exists is in `P` (König /\nHopcroft–Karp) — i.e. matching-decision is *not* hard. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.matchingCountHard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.matchingCountHard","kind":"opaque","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OptionBCountingTransfer.lean#L55-L56","doc":"Counting perfect matchings is `#P`-hard (Valiant). ","signatureChunk":0}]}